ing. Witness-depth sections below already carry full provenance.\n\nThis entry is BOUNDED — the whole graph is deliberately not inlined. Every node is reachable within a bounded number of expands: before concluding the perspective is silent on your subject, check the map and coverage, then expand the door whose axis would hold it (^Thematic for topics and areas, ^People for anyone, ^Documents for a call or memory, ^Unplaced for loose positions). Absence becomes signal only after the relevant door shows nothing.\n\n# The map — this graph's richest ground (top fidelity band)\n\n## ^Narrative_AntiSlackPositioning  [4 children · 20260310]\nTanya frames the product against Slack's real-time model. The anti-Slack label is the primary positioning thesis: every conversation should produce a persistent decision artifact.\n  decisions-under 1 · evidence 4 — expand ^Narrative_AntiSlackPositioning for the full child index\n\n# Coverage — narrated, from four directions\n\nActive: [ Position_ContextPreservationNextSprint · Next sprint focus: context preservation — linking decisions to t… ^Position_ContextPreservationNextSprint ] · [ Position_AntiPatternRealtimeChat · Real-time chat (Slack, Teams) is the named anti-pattern. The pro… ^Position_AntiPatternRealtimeChat ] — the newest witnessed work, one document each.\n\n# Doors — pick an axis\n\n[ ^Thematic — every area (0) by name ] [ ^People 0 ] [ ^Dimensions — 0 axes ] [ ^Documents 2 ] [ ^Unplaced 0 ]\nEach door expands to a complete axis: aswritten_expand(iris=[\"Thematic\"]) — same coords as this perspective. Nothing in the graph is outside every door.\n\n# Focus: Intake rota and pantry operating policies: fortnightly intake hand-offs with a 15-minute overlap, and pantry shelf restocking below one-third full, both effective November 1; participants Priya Holm and Dario Kent. (witness depth — per-call section)\n\n### Position_Sprint4ThesisProven\ntype: Position\nwitnessed: 20260322\nsource: Sample_Sprint4Retro_20260322\nTanya: '